  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "北歐音樂文化",
    "sub_ename": "NORTHERN EUROPEAN MUSIC CULTURE",
    "describe_ch": "北歐自古以來便擁有濃厚的音樂氛圍，許多人認為其獨特的自然環境造就了音樂的清新動人與觸動心靈。無論是流行音樂、電子音樂還是民謠，北歐音樂在全球音樂版圖上的重要性日益突出。本課程將專注於斯堪地那維亞半島（瑞典、丹麥、挪威）以及冰島的知名流行音樂藝術家、古典音樂家和重要的民間音樂。透過這些內容，我們將深入探討北歐音樂的風格與獨特性，並了解它們如何感動全球的聽眾。",
    "describe_eh": "Northern Europe has long been rich in musical atmosphere, with many believing that its unique natural environment has given rise to music that is fresh, captivating, and deeply moving. Whether in pop music, electronic music, or folk traditions, Northern European music is becoming increasingly significant on the global music landscape. This course will focus on notable popular music artists and classical musicians from the countries in Scandinavian Peninsula (Sweden, Denmark, Norway) and Iceland, as well as important folk music. Through this exploration, we will delve into the styles and uniqueness of Northern European music and understand how they resonate with audiences worldwide.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
